# Intentionally empty — unix has NO submodules.
#
# 2026-08-11: the five submodules here (I_cloud-data, II_tools, III_front-data,
# IV_cloud-configs, V_front-configs) were removed. cloud-master is the indexing
# path now: it holds committed RELATIVE symlinks to sibling working clones in
# ~/git, deliberately not submodules. See cloud-master/clone.sh — a submodule
# pins a commit and wants --recursive, which here meant cloud-master containing
# cloud containing cloud-master, plus private repos breaking init for anyone
# without those credentials.
#
# Nothing in unix read through those directories at runtime; they were pure
# index duplication of clones that already exist as siblings. The one real
# filesystem reference (ea_cloud-superapp/data/regen.sh) already goes via
# $HOME/git/cloud-infra/, not through a submodule path. No workflow checked them out
# either, so CI never depended on them.
#
# unix-ship-repo-workflow-engine.sh reconciles declaratively against this file:
# declared-but-unregistered gets `git submodule add`, registered-but-undeclared
# gets `git rm --cached`. So RE-ADDING A SECTION HERE RESURRECTS A SUBMODULE on
# the next ship. That is exactly how I_cloud-data kept reappearing staged.
# Add repos to cloud-master/repos.json instead.
